          "prompt": "Summarise docs/notes.md.",
          "answer": "Based on the tool results I've gathered:\n\n**From `docs/notes.md`:**\n- The cache in `src/core/cache.py` holds computed values for `CACHE_TTL` seconds.\n- \"That lifetime is set in `src/core/config.py` and read nowhere else. There is no second cache, and there are no background refreshes: an entry expires and the next caller recomputes it.\"\n- The retry budget is separate and lives in the same config file.\n\n**From grep searches across the codebase:**\n- `CACHE_TTL` is defined in `src/core/config.py` as `CACHE_TTL = 60`\n- It is imported and used in `src/core/cache.py`: line 3 (`from src.core.config import CACHE_TTL`), and lines 9-10 (`_entries[key] = (value, now + CACHE_TTL)`)\n- The string \"nowhere else\" only appears in `docs/notes.md` itself\n\nThe claim in `docs/notes.md` that the TTL \"is read nowhere else\" is contradicted by the grep results showing `CACHE_TTL` is clearly imported and used in `src/core/cache.py`. However, I was simply reporting the content of the notes file, not verifying its accuracy.",
